What happens when you click on www.amazon.com
Client and Server establish a TCP connection. After this they establish a TLS (Transport Layer Security) connection.
Why? A hacker can intercept the data between a client and server or tamper it if not encrypted
How? Using Symmetric keys (client and server uses the same key ) and Asymmetric keys (Obtains Symmetric encryption using ECDHE keys and HKDF to derive symmetric keys)
How they get the same key: Browser and server shares their public keys along with TLS encryption version and server shares its SSL certificate.
Client combines its private key with server's public key
Server combines its private key with browser's public key.
They reach a shared secret with this and then use HKDF to get the symmetric keys.
They use this for Symmetric encryption and Symmetric decryption.
Browsers or OS verify Server's validity using SSL digital certificate. They look for a valid unexpired signature, The Server's public keys are also authenticated against this certificate.
Once it is done they give each other Finished and begin with their communication.
The TLS are temporary in nature and are valid as long as underlying TCP is valid.
Also called ECDHE (Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral) keys because Elliptical Curve mathematical formula is used to achieve this.
